{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "or-scheduled-messages-2026-11-26",
		"name": "OpenRegister Scheduled Messages API",
		"description": "Messages scheduled on an object, listed and cancelled over HTTP (change send-at-on-the-messaging-leaf, task 3.2, the Newman half).\n\nAn administrator schedules an e-mail bound to a case two days ahead (POST /api/integrations/email/send with sendAt and object): 202, pending, a minted Message-ID. A past sendAt and one that is no date are 400, never read as now. GET /api/objects/{register}/{schema}/{id}/messages lists it for the administrator and for a reader who may read the case. The reader may not cancel the administrator's message (403: only the author or one who may update the object), but schedules and cancels their own. The administrator cancels theirs; a second cancel is 409, an unknown id 404, and the list reads both cancelled. On a case the reader may not read, listing and scheduling are 404, and nothing is stored.\n\nThe sweep never runs here: every sendAt is two days ahead, so no mail server is needed. Self-cleaning: it removes its cases, register, schemas and user.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"event": [
		{
			"listen": "prerequest",
			"script": {
				"type": "text/javascript",
				"exec": [
					"pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'OCS-APIRequest', value: 'true' });"
				]
			}
		}
	],
